      "writtenOn": "2024-06-20T10:18:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the current regex looks much better.\n\nHowever, I am not fully follow why a stateful parsing is more complicated.\n\nIn one dumpsys, it is guaranteed that we only see one full APF dump.\n\nWhat we can do is:\n1. we find prefix \"IpClient.wlan\" if we don\u0027t find it, throw\n2. we find the \"${counter name} : \", if we don\u0027t find, throw.\n3. if we find the counter name, we parse the counter value.\n\n\nThoughts?",
