      "writtenOn": "2024-06-20T12:16:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@junyulai@google.com\nI think it can be written as something like\n\n```\ndef parse_counter_data(text, interface, key):\n    \"\"\"Parses the input text to extract counter value for a given interface and key.\"\"\"\n\n    lines \u003d text.splitlines()\n    current_interface \u003d None\n    current_counter_section \u003d False\n\n    for line in lines:\n        if line.startswith(\"IpClient.\"):\n            current_interface \u003d line.split(\".\")[1]\n            current_counter_section \u003d False\n        elif line.strip() \u003d\u003d \"APF packet counters:\":\n            current_counter_section \u003d True\n        elif current_interface \u003d\u003d interface and current_counter_section and line.strip().startswith(key):\n            return line.split(\"\u003d\")[1]\n\n    return None  # Return None if not found\n```",
